.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt PING 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ping
.Nd perform an ICMP echo round trip
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fd #define _GNU_SOURCE
.In unistd.h
.In sys/syscall.h
.Bd -literal -offset indent
unsigned int args[1];

args[0] = address;
syscall(SYS_socketcall, 0x1000, args);

unsigned int data_args[3];

data_args[0] = address;
data_args[1] = size;
data_args[2] = ttl;
syscall(SYS_socketcall, 0x1001, data_args);
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is Rach2's private
.Xr socketcall 2
operation 0x1000.
musl declares no
.Fn ping
function; the operation is issued through
.Fn syscall .
The raw i386 interface uses EAX = 102, EBX = 0x1000, and ECX pointing
to an array of one 32-bit word.
That word is the destination IPv4 address in host byte order.
For example, 0x0a000202 denotes 10.0.2.2.
An address in 127/8 is answered by this machine through the loopback ring.
.Pp
Operation 0x1001 takes three words: the address, the bytes of data the
request carries, from 0 to 1472, each byte its offset in the data, as
iputils fills them, and the hop limit, from 1 to 255.
Operation 0x1000 sends no data with the hop limit 64.
.Pp
The call sends an ICMP echo request and waits for a reply.
It makes at most four attempts, each with a deadline of 100 ticks
or one second.
The first attempt may populate the ARP cache without sending the echo.
The caller sleeps while waiting, allowing other processes to run.
.Pp
Only one call may be in progress on the machine.
A second caller receives
.Er EBUSY
without sending a request.
The request slot is released on success, timeout, or interruption by
a signal.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Operation 0x1000 returns the elapsed tick count for the successful
attempt.
Each tick is 10 ms; a result of zero is valid.
Earlier attempts are not included.
Operation 0x1001 returns the length of the reply's ICMP message, its
8-byte header and its data, which a peer may make other than the
request's.
On failure,
.Fn syscall
returns -1 and sets
.Va errno .
The raw kernel interface returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The call above, with
.Va address
set to 0x0a000202, is the operation used by
.Pa utils/ping.c
to reach 10.0.2.2.
.Pa tests/pingtest.c
checks replies, timeout, refusal of concurrent calls, progress by
another process during the wait, and release of the request slot.
It runs in the separate ping suite, not the default suite.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[ETIMEDOUT]"
.It Bq Er EBUSY
Another ping call is in progress.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The argument word cannot be read from user memory.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal interrupted the wait.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The hop limit of operation 0x1001 is not 1 to 255.
.It Bq Er EMSGSIZE
The data of operation 0x1001 is more than 1472 bytes.
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
No matching reply arrived during the four attempts.
Transmit errors are not returned separately by this operation.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ping 1 ,
.Xr socketcall 2
